  "slug": "learning-biology-small-c2ee",
  "summary": "Constrained generative and screening models are now paired with filtering and experimental checks on predicted hits in 2026 publications.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the use of explicit constraints to steer molecular generation and screening, with outputs carried forward to filtering or experimental tests. PharmaDiff conditions 3D de novo generation on pharmacophores, and SF-GA uses fragment-synergy guidance to redesign predicted P-gp substrates into synthetically accessible predicted nonsubstrates. PFM applies flow matching with a perturbed conditional probability path to pocket-conditioned 3D generation. On the screening side, a rule-defined 2D PEG ligand library of about 123M generated and roughly 50M retained structures supports virtual screening, and QRxVision encodes multimodal drug parameters as QR code images for kinase target assignment. The newer element relative to generative-model papers is filtering and experimental confirmation rather than architecture. A GNN, docking and MD pipeline identified carvedilol as a partial THRβ agonist, and this is the only item reporting wet-lab validation, confirmed by TR-FRET and cell lipid assays.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-11"
}
